      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing your hormone dosage isn't a safe or effective solution because the liver enzymes induced by St. John's wort can make the pill work too poorly regardless of the amount taken. Relying on self-adjusting medication doses to counteract drug interactions is risky and can lead to serious health issues like unexpected pregnancy or hormonal imbalances. It is much safer to choose a different natural therapy for your mood, such as a pescatarian diet rich in essential omega-3 fatty acids, and discuss your concerns with a doctor for personalized, safe treatment options.",
      "source": "target",
